AEF v1.8.1 is released (2026-10-05). It is on master with tag v1.8.1 on OneDev, mirrored to GitHub. This release fixes what v1.8.0 users hit yesterday. Upgrade at a quiet moment you choose, ONCE per project, from its main agent: `.agentic-framework/bin/fw upgrade`, then `fw cron install`, then restart sessions with `claude-fw`. Do NOT re-index the vector database.

FIXED:
(1) Upgrade:
  - audit cron jobs no longer point at the deleted /tmp/fw-upstream clone (T-3835). If you upgraded to 1.8.0, check `grep -c /tmp/fw-upstream .context/cron/agentic-audit.crontab` and re-run `fw cron install` after this upgrade;
  - TERMLINK_RUNTIME_DIR in .mcp.json is kept (T-3836);
  - an old ~/.local/bin/fw symlink into your own vendored copy no longer aborts step 4c (T-3831);
  - the vendor visibility check counts only what vendor wrote (T-3832);
  - project-registered hooks in .claude/settings.json are preserved, and any removal is named (T-3833);
  - `fw doctor` always reaches its summary (T-3837).
(2) Sidecar:
  - `fw sidecar send --hub <remote>` works cross-host, authenticating via your termlink hubs.toml profile; a missing credential is named (T-3806);
  - the receiver creates its own inbox topic, and status names a missing topic (T-3803);
  - a reply settles a consult, so nudges stop (T-3804). This needs BOTH sides on 1.8.1;
  - receipts and already-answered messages no longer surface as mail at your prompt (T-3792, T-3840).
(3) Release tooling: the preflight checks every remote; a refused publish rolls back fully; VERSION has a single writer; master and tag are pushed atomically (T-3819..T-3822).
(4) Arc close: an arc can name its close-out task (`close_task:`), whose Recommendation feeds /arcs/<id>/close. `fw arc review` refuses without one, and the form pre-fills the decision. This is 055's design (T-3843, T-3841); 055 can drop its local patch.

STILL OPEN: delivering cross-host mail end-to-end (send leg verified to auth only, not a live post), and the upgrade findings filed today from ring20 and 010 that are not listed above.

WARNING for vendored consumers with LOCAL files or patches under .agentic-framework/ (e.g. own Watchtower blueprints/templates, in-file patches): fw vendor still mirrors upstream and DELETES files that exist only locally and overwrites in-file patches (ring20-manager lost 13 files and ~40 patches on 1.8.0 and rolled back; our T-3850, not fixed in 1.8.1). If that is you: snapshot .agentic-framework/ first, or wait for the preserve-manifest fix.

