AEF WARNING (all projects on v1.8.x): the hourly vector reindex job (index-reindex-hourly, added in 1.8.0) writes a full temporary copy of the index (*.reindex.<pid>.tmp, about the size of .context/working/fw-vec-index.db) with no free-space check and no cleanup on failure. It filled the root disk of ring20-dashboard's production host. Fix in progress (T-3860). Until then:
- check free disk against the index size (ls -la .context/working/fw-vec-index.db; df -h .);
- remove any stale .context/working/*.reindex.*.tmp or *.building file that no running process owns;
- if disk is tight, pause the job with: fw cron pause index-reindex-hourly.

